# 🤖 Machine Learning Models

The project uses two custom YOLO models.

## 1. Number Plate Detection Model

File:

```text
models/number_plate_detector.pt
```

Purpose:

```text
Vehicle Image
      ↓
YOLO Number Plate Detection
      ↓
Number Plate Bounding Box
      ↓
Cropped Number Plate
```

---

## 2. Traffic Violation Detection Model

File:

```text
models/violation_detector.pt
```

Purpose:

```text
Vehicle Image
      ↓
YOLO Violation Detection
      ↓
Violation Class
      ↓
Fine Lookup
```

---

# 🗄️ Database Structure

## User Database

The user database stores vehicle owner information.

Example fields:

```text
id
user_name
vehicle_reg
vehicle_type
mobile_number
```

Example:

```text
Name          : Omkar
Vehicle Reg   : TS09AB1234
Vehicle Type  : Scooty
Mobile        : 9876543210
```

---

## Challan Database

The challan database stores traffic violation and fine information.

Example:

| Violation   |  Fine |
| ----------- | ----: |
| Triple Ride | ₹1000 |
| No Parking  |  ₹100 |
| No Helmet   |  ₹300 |
| Overspeed   |  ₹500 |

The database also stores generated challan records.

---

# ⚙️ Installation

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/nazneen-fatima/Traffic_challan_Project.git
```

Navigate to the project:

```bash
cd Traffic_challan_Project
```

---

## 2. Create a Virtual Environment

For Windows:

```bash
python -m venv challan_venv
```

Activate the environment:

```bash
challan_venv\Scripts\activate
```

---

## 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# 🔐 Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root.

Example:

```text
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key

MYSQL_HOST=localhost
MYSQL_USER=your_mysql_username
MYSQL_PASSWORD=your_mysql_password
```

### ⚠️ Security

**Never upload `.env` to GitHub.**

The project `.gitignore` contains:

```text
.env
```

so that API keys and database credentials remain private.

---

# 🗃️ MySQL Configuration

Make sure MySQL is installed and running before starting the application.

Create the required databases and tables for:

* Vehicle owner information
* Vehicle registration details
* Traffic violations
* Fine amounts
* Challan records

Update your `.env` file with the correct MySQL credentials.

---

# 🚀 Running the Application

## Main Application

To run the main application:

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

---

## WhatsApp-Enabled Application

To run the separate WhatsApp-enabled UI:

```bash
streamlit run "app1[whatsapp].py"
```

This version provides the WhatsApp option in the Streamlit interface.

---

# 📱 WhatsApp Workflow

The WhatsApp-enabled application uses a Click-to-Chat URL.

The workflow is:

```text
Challan Generated
       ↓
WhatsApp Button
       ↓
WhatsApp Opens
       ↓
Challan Message Pre-filled
       ↓
User Reviews Message
       ↓
User Presses Send
```

This implementation is intended for **project demonstration and testing**.

It does not automatically send messages without user interaction.

---

